          "question": {
            "text": "Suppose that the side lengths of a triangle are three consecutive integers and one of the angles is twice another. The number of such triangles is/are",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "owQa1",
              "text": "<math> <mn>1</mn> </math>",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "I7EQn",
              "text": "<math> <mn>0</mn></math>",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "FTACW",
              "text": "<math> <mn>4</mn></math>",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "70k52",
              "text": "<math> <mn>2</mn></math>",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Let <math> <mtext>B</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>A</mtext> </math> and <math> <mtext>B</mtext><mtext>D</mtext> </math> be the bisector of angle <math> <mrow> <mtext>B</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> then<br /><br /><math><mrow><mtext>CD</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>ab</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> <mtext>AD</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>bc</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Now,&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mo>Δ</mo> <mtext>ABC</mtext> <mo>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</mo> <mo>Δ</mo> <mtext>BDC</mtext> </mrow> </math> are similar, so<br /><br /><math><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mtext>BC</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>AC</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>CD</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>BC</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>⇒</mo> <msup> <mtext>a</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>ab</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>b</mtext> <mo>&nbsp;⇒&nbsp;</mo> <msup> <mtext>b</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>a</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;......(i)<br /><br />Since, <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo></mrow> </math> Either <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </math> or <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo> </math> if <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo> </math> then [From Eq.(i)]<br /><br /><math><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"><mrow><mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>⇒</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/fvvvvvv.JPG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 169px;\" /><br /><math><mtext>c</mtext> </math> is integer <math><mrow><mo>⇒</mo></mrow></math> <math> <mrow><mtext>a</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>c</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow> </math> but then, no triangle will form.<br />If <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> then obviously <math> <mrow> <mtext>c</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> and then, [from Eq. (i)]<br /><br /><math> <msup> <mfenced> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </mfenced> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mfenced> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </mfenced> </math><br /><br /><math> <mo>⇒</mo><msup> <mtext>a</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>or</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>a</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn> </math><br /><br /><math> <mo>∴</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>a</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>c</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn> </math> is the only possible solution.",
